{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1452748-how-you-usually-picture-pookas-in-your-table-dr-moreau-style-furry-nekomimi","id":1452748,"title":"How you usually picture pookas in your table? Dr. Moreau style? Furry? \"Nekomimi\"?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-18T04:11:03-07:00","id":1452748,"title":"How you usually picture pookas in your table? Dr. Moreau style? Furry? \"Nekomimi\"?","content":"I think the nekomimi and furry style are the most prevalent in official art. Some pookas are portrayed as literally having animal heads and humanoid bodies. Other arts like second edition corebook are more close to nekomimi, with the pooka being mostly human but with animals ears and few other chracteristics, but mostly cute or normal, not bizarre. And a few art portray them a as Dr.Moreau style, a mismatch of human and animal, with a very uncanny valley apperance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Personally I don't like the furry depictions a lot, pookas already can turn into animals, so I don't see much appeal in looking a lot like animals in their human form too. So I mostly use the &quot;catgirl&quot; descriptions, but not necessarily cute, just making the human characteristics a bit more animalesque, like long nose for a eagle pooka, or flat face for a owl pooka.<br /> <br /> <br /> But sometimes, for more somber games and one-shots I do like Dr.Moreau style pookas, with beaks instead of noses, talons, feathers in all the body, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T20:36:47-07:00","id":1452851,"title":"","content":"Generally something along the lines of the beast people that are common in a lot of modern fantasy anime. At least the ones were they all look like people with animal ears and occasionally tails as opposed to the ones where they have ludicrous levels of sexual dimorphism (I'm looking at you, Seton Academy). <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T00:21:48-07:00","id":1452869,"title":"","content":"When it comes to Changeling kiths, I try to map them to various fairy tale characters or fairy legends in general. However they are described in those tales, or how the Golden Age illustrators choose to depict them (Arthur Rackham, Kay Nielsen, Edmund Dulac, Maxfield Parrish, etc.) is what I go with. I am fortunate enough to have the entire Enchanted World series of books from Time-Life, and they have gorgeous art. So I have plenty of material.<br /> <br /> For pookas, that is generally any animal helper (it looks just like an animal), any animal that wears clothes and therefore slightly anthropomorphized, or a mostly human looking figure with one or a few animal traits (often hidden at first glance, but can be spotted if one looks close enough). In terms of their regular Mien, it's probably one of the latter two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-10T18:48:52-07:00","id":1454667,"title":"","content":"I love this question. Had to google what &quot;nekomimi&quot; means.<br /> <br /> To me what matters is that everyone is comfortable and has fun on the table, so assuming one player doesn't trigger another one it's all fine. I have no personal preference about how to portray a pooka, and I don't really mind mixing things up (for example, allowing different characters have different &quot;styles&quot; - one pooka may be more alien while another one might be mostly human).<br /> <br /> On my next game I'll play a bunnygirl pooka (so, closer to the nekomimi thing), but in a family friendly way, nothing adult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26930-syrian-kobold","name":"syrian kobold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26930_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T19:44:43-07:00","id":1454780,"title":"","content":"I tend to do a bit of a Seelie/Unseelie divide. Seelie Pooka are mostly in the &quot;nekomimi&quot; mode - they basically look like humans with some minor animal features (ears, tails, wings, horns, etc). A Seelie Pooka could fit in at a cosplay convention without seeming too out of place. Unseelie Pooka often have more prominent animalistic features, and would be more moving into &quot;furry&quot; territory. They'd be more likely to have animal muzzles or other extreme animal features (their arms and hands or legs would be full animalistic or such). If a Pooka spends more time in one Legacy or another their animal traits will slowly grow or decline over time. But it's not a hard rule though and you can have furry Seelie Pooka and nekomimi Unseelie Pooka, they just tend to be somewhat unusual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-12-2021, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T03:31:04-07:00","id":1454873,"title":"","content":"The hybrid children from the Sweet Tooth series are a fair depiction of Pooka Childlings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-21T20:24:55-07:00","id":1455343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1452748-how-you-usually-picture-pookas-in-your-table-dr-moreau-style-furry-nekomimi?p=1454780#post1454780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to do a bit of a Seelie/Unseelie divide. Seelie Pooka are mostly in the &amp;quot;nekomimi&amp;quot; mode - they basically look like humans with some minor animal features (ears, tails, wings, horns, etc). A Seelie Pooka could fit in at a cosplay convention without seeming too out of place. Unseelie Pooka often have more prominent animalistic features, and would be more moving into &amp;quot;furry&amp;quot; territory. They'd be more likely to have animal muzzles or other extreme animal features (their arms and hands or legs would be full animalistic or such). If a Pooka spends more time in one Legacy or another their animal traits will slowly grow or decline over time. But it's not a hard rule though and you can have furry Seelie Pooka and nekomimi Unseelie Pooka, they just tend to be somewhat unusual.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much how I do it as well. But with how much they embrace their Fae nature versus their human nature with mentally healthy Changelings somewhere between the two and it can change from day to day. This is the only Kith I do this with however as Pooka are the shapechangers of the Changeling and are naturally a bit more mercurial than the other Kiths.<br /> But Seelie and Unseelie is actually a good way of separating it, wish I had thought of that. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart","name":"KnightFenrirWulfhart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T18:13:27-07:00","id":1457532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rucun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1452748-how-you-usually-picture-pookas-in-your-table-dr-moreau-style-furry-nekomimi#post1452748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But sometimes, for more somber games and one-shots I do like Dr.Moreau style pookas, with beaks instead of noses, talons, feathers in all the body, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this makes for more somber games. Sobriety is far more on their behavior than their appearance.<br /> <br /> As any other kith, Pookas are fairies, not lab experiments or &quot;natural&quot; hybrids. They're dreams, usually considerably old dreams (as far as Seeming is concerned). Those can be certainly unsettling, and sometimes Moreau-style, but more frequently they would be the other two description because they ARE far more common in legends and folklore, &quot;nekomimi&quot;, not necessarily cute ones, for animal-fairies that disguise among humans, and &quot;furry&quot; for the many magical animals that learn to walk on two legs.<br /> <br /> Bizarre amalgams, as far as fairy tales go, are far more frequently monsters that would be either Chimeras or Bygones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T07:52:38-07:00","id":1457712,"title":"","content":"I usually portray them as humans with animal features that clearly show what their animal nature is but not going to actual furry territory. This can be affected by Merits/Flaws taken by the Pooka\u2019s player. Pretty much like the official art in Kithbook: Pooka, especially those drawn by Melissa Uran.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T14:56:49-07:00","id":1518324,"title":"","content":"I definitely prefer anthropomorphic animals, cause that's what I associate with fairytales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T16:02:18-07:00","id":1518330,"title":"","content":"Changelings are individuals. I prefer the take of the illustrations of the books. But many things are possible and few are all that rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T17:56:36-07:00","id":1519061,"title":"","content":"Whatever and whichever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}